Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
------------------------------------------------  
• "disease_code": filter to KIRP (Kidney Renal Papillary Cell Carcinoma)  
• "clinical_stage": cancer stage grouping – must be NOT NULL  
• "case_barcode": patient identifier – used to JOIN the two tables and to hash‑split into train / test with FARM_FINGERPRINT  
• "project_short_name": quick sanity check that the sample really belongs to TCGA‑KIRP (value should be ‘TCGA‑KIRP’)  
• "gene_name": select mitochondrial genes of interest: ‘MT‑CO1’, ‘MT‑CO2’, ‘MT‑CO3’  
• "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ": expression value to average, measure distance, etc.  

Typical conditions that will be used later  
• WHERE "disease_code" = 'KIRP'  
• WHERE "clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL  
• WHERE "gene_name" IN ('MT‑CO1','MT‑CO2','MT‑CO3')  
• ABS(MOD(FARM_FINGERPRINT("case_barcode"),10)) < 9   → 90 % train  
• ABS(MOD(FARM_FINGERPRINT("case_barcode"),10)) = 9   → 10 % test  

Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries  
-------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Description: See all disease codes present in the clinical table (sanity check for ‘KIRP’)
SELECT DISTINCT "disease_code"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Count patients that belong to KIRP and already have a non‑null clinical stage
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "kirp_with_stage"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"
WHERE "disease_code" = 'KIRP'
  AND "clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: List the distinct clinical stages found for KIRP cases
SELECT DISTINCT "clinical_stage"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"
WHERE "disease_code" = 'KIRP'
  AND "clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Peek at a few KIRP patient records with their stage and vital status
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "clinical_stage",
       "vital_status",
       "gender"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"
WHERE "disease_code" = 'KIRP'
  AND "clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Check whether the three mitochondrial genes exist in the RNA‑seq table
SELECT DISTINCT "gene_name"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION"
WHERE "gene_name" ILIKE 'MT-CO%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Retrieve a few expression rows for MT‑CO3 across KIRP samples
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "sample_barcode",
       "gene_name",
       "HTSeq__FPKM_UQ"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION"
WHERE "gene_name" = 'MT-CO3'
  AND "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-KIRP'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Join clinical & expression tables to see MT‑CO1 expression along with stage
SELECT c."case_barcode",
       c."clinical_stage",
       r."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" AS "mt_co1_fpkm_uq"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"    c
JOIN "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION" r
  ON c."case_barcode" = r."case_barcode"
WHERE c."disease_code" = 'KIRP'
  AND c."clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
  AND r."gene_name" = 'MT-CO1'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Pull all three gene expressions for one random KIRP patient (pivot‑style view)
SELECT r."case_barcode",
       MAX(CASE WHEN r."gene_name" = 'MT-CO1' THEN r."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "MT_CO1",
       MAX(CASE WHEN r."gene_name" = 'MT-CO2' THEN r."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "MT_CO2",
       MAX(CASE WHEN r."gene_name" = 'MT-CO3' THEN r."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ" END) AS "MT_CO3"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION" r
WHERE r."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-KIRP'
  AND r."gene_name" IN ('MT-CO1','MT-CO2','MT-CO3')
GROUP BY r."case_barcode"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Demonstrate FARM_FINGERPRINT‑based 90/10 split on KIRP patients with stage
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "clinical_stage",
       ABS(MOD(FARM_FINGERPRINT("case_barcode"),10)) AS "hash_mod_10",
       CASE WHEN ABS(MOD(FARM_FINGERPRINT("case_barcode"),10)) < 9
            THEN 'TRAIN' ELSE 'TEST' END AS "set_type"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"
WHERE "disease_code" = 'KIRP'
  AND "clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Description: Compute the mean MT‑CO3 expression per clinical stage for the TRAIN cohort only
SELECT c."clinical_stage",
       AVG(r."HTSeq__FPKM_UQ") AS "avg_mt_co3_fpkm_uq"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_BIOCLIN_V0"."CLINICAL"    c
JOIN "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION" r
  ON c."case_barcode" = r."case_barcode"
WHERE c."disease_code" = 'KIRP'
  AND c."clinical_stage" IS NOT NULL
  AND r."gene_name" = 'MT-CO3'
  AND ABS(MOD(FARM_FINGERPRINT(c."case_barcode"),10)) < 9   -- training set only
GROUP BY c."clinical_stage"
LIMIT 20;
```
